# bash-debugtrap  (generated by harness/probes.py)
Q: is the DEBUG trap a usable CommandStarted/Finished source?

For each typed line the probe counts how many DEBUG firings occur.

=== typed: echo one ===
DEBUG fired 2 time(s):
   DEBUG cmd=[echo one] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[printf "\033]0;%s@%s:%s\007" "${USER}" "${HOSTNAME%%.*}" "${PWD/#$HOME/\~}"] rc=0
=== typed: printf 'a\n' | wc -l ===
DEBUG fired 3 time(s):
   DEBUG cmd=[printf 'a\n'] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[wc -l] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[printf "\033]0;%s@%s:%s\007" "${USER}" "${HOSTNAME%%.*}" "${PWD/#$HOME/\~}"] rc=0
=== typed: true && echo chained ===
DEBUG fired 3 time(s):
   DEBUG cmd=[true] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo chained] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[printf "\033]0;%s@%s:%s\007" "${USER}" "${HOSTNAME%%.*}" "${PWD/#$HOME/\~}"] rc=0
=== typed: echo A; echo B; echo C ===
DEBUG fired 4 time(s):
   DEBUG cmd=[echo A] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo B] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo C] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[printf "\033]0;%s@%s:%s\007" "${USER}" "${HOSTNAME%%.*}" "${PWD/#$HOME/\~}"] rc=0
=== typed: for i in 1 2 3; do echo L$i; done ===
DEBUG fired 7 time(s):
   DEBUG cmd=[for i in 1 2 3] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo L$i] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[for i in 1 2 3] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo L$i] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[for i in 1 2 3] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[echo L$i] rc=0
   DEBUG cmd=[printf "\033]0;%s@%s:%s\007" "${USER}" "${HOSTNAME%%.*}" "${PWD/#$HOME/\~}"] rc=0
